  the coupling: g5 phi^2 psibar psi, g5 = m_e0 kappa (DIM-5 operator, [g5]=mass^-1, [kappa]=mass^-2)

1-LOOP beta-functions (rigorous):
  gamma_me   = 3 alpha/2pi = 0.00348      (QED mass anomalous dim -- STANDARD)
  beta_mphi2 = (kappa/pi^2) m_e0^4       (electron CW loop induces the dyad mass; LINEAR in kappa)
  beta_kappa ~ (3 alpha/2pi) kappa + O(kappa^2, lambda kappa)   (QED dressing of the phi^2(psibar psi) vertex)

WHY 1-LOOP CANNOT PIN T_c:
  T_c = m_e0 sqrt(3(L-1)/2pi^2), L-1 = ln(m_e0^2/mu^2) - 3/2. The overall kappa CANCELS
  (both m_phi^2(0) and the thermal Dm^2 ~ kappa). So T_c's mu-dependence is ENTIRELY the log bracket.
  1-loop running of the SOURCE S(mu)=kappa(mu) m_e0(mu)^4:
    dlnS/dln_mu ~ beta_k/k + 4 gamma_me ~ 0.0174  (O(alpha), TINY)
  A PMS stationary point (dT_c/dln_mu=0) from this curvature needs the linear log ~ 1/(dlnS/dlnmu):
    log* ~ 1/0.0174 ~ 57  ->  mu*/m_e ~ e^-57 = 1e-25  -- UNPHYSICAL
  => the O(alpha) coupling-running does NOT fix the leading-log. T_c stays ambiguous at 1-loop.

